# Training manual note: COA / micro catalog

When building the **end-of-project training manual**, include a short section on **Quality → COA / micro catalog** with **screenshots** of the catalog table page.

Explain columns the same way as in product Q&A:

## # (order)
Display order only — lower numbers appear first in the FPS catalog picker and on product COA / hold-release lines. Not a test ID.

## Flags
- **COA** — Include this test by default on customer COAs when added to an FPS.
- **On** — Active in the catalog. Off hides it from the FPS picker without deleting.

## Kind
How the result is judged:
- **Numeric range (min–max)** — Must fall between Min and Max.
- **Numeric minimum (e.g. NLT)** — Must be at least Min.
- **Pass / fail (text)** — Text like Pass / Fail / Negative; often Pass/Fail on customer COA.
- **Text only** — Free text (e.g. `≤ 10,000 CFU/g`); no auto pass/fail from numbers.

Also mention: **Specification** prints on the COA; **Typical result** prefills hold-release result entry.

UI surface: `slurp_ui/templates/slurp_ui/quality/coa_test_catalog.html` (route `quality_coa_test_catalog`).

